    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The runoff election winner in the Texas contest was determined by a clear margin of victory, with the politician benefiting from the timing of endorsement that clarified the outcome. This result, a historical precedent broken, occurred despite the financial advantage held by the outspent incumbent. The nominee will now face the Democratic representative in a future contest that could influence control of the U.S. Senate, presenting voters with a high-stakes battle for Senate control.",
